Author: vvondruska <vaclav@re-cinq.com>
Date:   Fri Sep 11 16:17:50 2026 +0200

    fix(transport): call onConnect, and make both hooks safe

    T015. onConnect was declared on HalEngineConfig, forwarded through
    createHalEngine, declared again on HalServerOptions - and then left out
    of the deps object the connection handler receives, so it never fired.
    onDisconnect is forwarded on the adjacent line and works, which is why
    four documents could claim both worked.

    It runs on a microtask rather than inline: a synchronous throw in the
    connection listener corrupts an already-upgraded socket. A microtask
    rather than setImmediate because it drains before the loop can deliver an
    inbound frame, which is what "before the first message" requires.

    Both hooks widen to void | Promise<void> and route through one runHook
    that logs {sessionId, error} and swallows. onDisconnect was called bare
    inside a close listener, where a rejection ends the process under Node's
    defaults. Promise.resolve rather than instanceof Promise, so a thenable
    from another realm is absorbed too.

    Two new test files. The createServer one pins the omission itself: drop
    the forwarded line and it fails while the handler tests stay green,
    which is the shape the original defect had.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CyFimiuBEQXWWBktCx6gHE

